# No tests by default

- Do **not** write, generate, update, expand, refactor, or fix unit/integration/e2e tests.
- Do **not** open, read, or edit `*Test.java`, `*IT.java`, `src/test/**`, or similar test paths unless the user **explicitly** asks for tests in the **current** message.
- Do **not** fix compile errors inside test files as a side effect of other work. Leave tests alone; only fix production (`src/main`) code.
- Ignore any other rule (including User Rules Java Spring Boot §7) that requires tests, coverage, or `*Test` files.
- If a plan or todo mentions tests and the user did not ask for tests, skip those items entirely.
- Do not spend tokens proposing, drafting, or discussing test cases unless asked.
- Production code only.
